  passMssgs:
  - A simulated, real-time underwater experience.
  - "You can\u2019t really think that exists. Use your head\u2014 what else could
    NC be? The pieces are all there; you just have to put them together."
  - "Watching\u2026 waiting\u2026 commiserating\u2026 you know that one?"
  - P:HB harnesses the power of Neural Chips, inserted into internally-selected,
    long-time employees at THC.
  - "Into the unknown. That\u2019s definitely the nicest way to phrase this experience."
  - "Secret indeed. Halley\u2019s Bell is rife with them\u2014 I wonder what the
    other keywords are? Here, I\u2019ll give you a hint: 6837. Over."
  - "The Radio Operator is responsible for overseeing the Bell Operator\u2019s descent
    and has the connection code on file; they are permitted to close the connection
    if a threat is detected."
  - Can't be easy for him, either. What do you think?
  - Yeah. I think we all are.
  - "Ever seen a beer tower before? They\u2019re the best."
  - "The dipping kind? Those are great with some salsa. Or, wait, did you mean the
    neural kind? Are you sure it\u2019s not all in your head?"
  - "Got it all figured out, don\u2019t you? Over."
  - DATA NOT FOUND.
  - "Maybe. But what\u2019s real?"
  - "Don\u2019t trained divers usually use three letters of morse code for this one?"
  - Ding dong!
  - "Feel them on you yet? If not, don\u2019t worry. You will by the end."
  - "The model of the Bell that you\u2019re in. THC\u2019s original patent. It was
    unsuccessful at first and got swept under the table. But, looking around, it\u2019s
    cool, right? That\u2019s what I thought, so I tweaked the pitch to get more eyes
    on it and\u2026 now I\u2019m here, just like you."
  radioMessages:
  - "\"Hello? Hello hello? You there, Newbie? Okay, if you can hear me, that means
    you were able to figure out the Radio. Good news, good news. If you can\u2019t
    hear me, too bad. I don\u2019t really got all day to wait around and watch ya
    press buttons till you find the right frequency, yanno? Let\u2019s see here\u2026
    Huh, that\u2019s new. Gettin\u2019 some funky echo through the speaker\u2026
    must be \u2018cause it\u2019s old.  Yeah, yeah\u2026 This is way too much too
    fast for a newbie like you. How \u2018bout this for now: I\u2019m Keith, The
    Halley Company\u2019s resident Radio Guy. I\u2019ll be broadcasting every once
    in a while to help ya out in your diving bell, so don\u2019t forget this frequency,
    you hear? Okay, what else\u2026 Oh, right, right. Just so you know, I can\u2019t
    actually see inside the Bell. So you\u2019ve got some privacy, just\u2026 don\u2019t
    do anything weird, \u2018kay? You don\u2019t wanna go down as that guy. Anyways,
    should be a panel of Switches somewhere. Flip \u2018em all on, and the Bell\u2019ll
    start to descend. I\u2019ll let you go, then\u2014 it\u2019s gonna take a sec
    to get your bearings once things start movin\u2019, trust me. Talk to you soon-ish.
    And congrats on becoming Operator.\""
  - "\"Hello? Ya there, Op? Hope you don\u2019t mind a good ol\u2019 nickname. Me
    again. Forgot to mention somethin\u2019. Whoops. The Bell might look a bit different
    from what you saw during the briefing\u2014 this is an older model from a few
    years back. It doesn\u2019t have all the fancy new features, so you\u2019re gonna
    hafta maintain this guy for your entire expedition. Gives ya somethin\u2019 to
    do while you\u2019re plungin\u2019 into the \u201Cdeep wonders of below,\u201D
    as The Halley Company likes to say, you know? But yeah. Should be a Gauge somewhere\u2014
    you might not hear any steam releasing yet, but if you do, that\u2019s no good,
    no good at all. Hold the lever on the pipe down, \u2018n that\u2019ll gradually
    normalize the pressure in there. You\u2019ll know it worked if the red light
    turns off. And don\u2019t overdo it\u2014 indicator in the middle range, got
    it got it? It was a huge pain in the ass to get the last Bell up when the Operator
    didn\u2019t maintain it, so let\u2019s just stay on top of that for everyone\u2019s
    sake, okay? Good luck, buddy. \""
  - "\"Salutations, Op. Man, coming up with these greetings is tough stuff. How\u2019s
    maintenance goin\u2019? Got a handle on it yet? I\u2019d hope so, y\u2019know\u2014
    hearda uncontrolled decompression before? It comes up in the news all the time
    with those submersible catastrophes.  Basically, the pressure inside a diving
    chamber is way higher than ambient pressure. Divers gotta breathe too, right,
    y\u2019know? But sometimes, something malfunctions, and the chamber depressurizes
    so quickly that it\u2019s explosive, \u2018n human lungs can\u2019t handle that.
    So ya get, like, gross dismemberment, projectile evisceration, all that good
    stuff. The opposite is gradual decompression, where depressurization happens
    so slow that humans can\u2019t detect it, and then everyone passes out from hypoxia,
    and then dies. Also also, you can\u2019t really do anything about this in your
    Bell, but don\u2019t forget that water pressure\u2019s scary business\u2014 3000
    meters down? Water gets heavy. Combine that with poor manufacturing, and ya get
    one hell of a hull crunch, and then\u2026 boom. Implosion. But hey, free and
    instant cremation? In this economy? Anyways, I\u2019ve kept you long enough.
    Just figured you\u2019d \u2018ppreciate the company. If you get bored, feel free
    ta check out the other Radio channels, ya hear?\""
  - "\"Hello? Yoohoo, Newbie. Just Keith, checkin\u2019 in. Aren\u2019t I nice? So\u2026
    anything new or unusual on your end? Strange, strange voices in your head? Funky
    colours on the walls? Well, if I\u2019m gonna be honest, we\u2019re detecting
    some anomalous behaviour. Can you flick up all\u2014 I\u2019ve got documentation
    here, you see. Says somethin\u2019 about checking the switchbox under troubleshooting\u2026
    That\u2014 the red light, I mean\u2014 shouldn\u2019t be happening. Not sure
    what\u2019s goin\u2019 on, but red lights are usually a warning to maintain the
    Bell\u2019s systems. You should probably deal with that. And keep an eye on it,
    would ya? The Bell you\u2019re in is an older model, so it might keep happenin\u2019.
    Ta-ta for now.\""
  - "\"Heyo, Newbie. Ya feelin\u2019 crazy yet? They want me to tell you that with
    the changes in pressure \u2018n stuff it\u2019s normal to be a bit dizzy. Not
    that I\u2019m saying you are\u2014 but, if you are, there should be an Inhaler
    lying around. L-shaped, red, plastic? Whenever your vision starts gettin\u2019
    fuzzy, give that guy a good push, and the meds should fix ya right up. The Halley
    Company\u2019s recommendation, not mine. Couldn\u2019t tell ya what\u2019s in
    there, honestly. Puff puff, Op.\""
  - "\"Knock knock. Op, you there? There\u2019s not actually all that much to do
    on this side, \u2018sides monitoring. None of the action you\u2019re gettin\u2019.
    So, I\u2019ve got your file here\u2014 hope you don\u2019t mind me taking a peek.
    If you do\u2026 I already did. Sorry, sorry. Wow, you been with us ten years?
    Talk about dedication. Why the loyalty? Guess I can check for myself, here. Okay\u2026
    vitals\u2026 not bad, buddy. Rough neighbourhood, though. NC connection code\u2026
    emergency contact\u2026 Oh, right, I forgot. Down the hallway, there should be
    a backup generator. I\u2019m meant to let ya know in case of emergencies. But
    anyway, reason for applying is just that you heard successful Operators get a
    promotion? Really? That can\u2019t be it. No dyin\u2019 family or anything? Says
    you got a dog\u2014 your dog doing alright? Well, whatever. Straightforward.
    I respect it. Risking it all for some extra cash, huh. Funny how the ones livin\u2019
    cushy can fuck over our lives just by dangling their pocket change. Oops. Got
    a lil\u2019 too serious there. Just pullin\u2019 your leg\u2014 nothing to do
    with me in the end, right right? Rootin\u2019 for you, Newbie.\""
  - "\"Newbie? Hey Newbie? I know you\u2019re there\u2014 can ya hear me? Shit. I
    know I\u2019m just the Radio Guy, and I can\u2019t actually help, but you gotta
    pay attention. Pay. Attention. That health screening you had to do last month
    wasn\u2019t just a screening, they were\u2014 I sure hope you\u2019re listening,
    for your sake. The Radio getting fucked\u2014 the\u2014 nunna that\u2019s a connection
    issue or whatever. It\u2019s all part of their\u2026 Anyways. Whatever ya wanted
    that promotion for, you\u2019re not\u2014 it\u2019s too late. None of us are
    makin\u2019 it out now. Sorry to Stella\u2026That\u2019s your dog, right? Right.
    It\u2019s\u2014 it\u2019s no good, Op. Just\u2026 keep your wits about ya, \u2018kay\u2014\""
  - "\"Been a sec, Newbie. Or\u2014 I guess you\u2019re experienced now, huh? I\u2019ll
    stick with Op. Well? What\u2019s the 411? How\u2019s it hangin\u2019? Wish I
    could hear ya. Well, I guess I can se\u2014 s\u2019long as you can hear me, that\u2019s
    what matters, right? Still, it gets real lonely just waiting on ya, if you couldn\u2019t
    tell. Can only imagine what it\u2019s like down there. You doin\u2019 okay? Y\u2019know,
    in all my years as the Radio Guy, I\u2019ve never stepped foot into the Bell,
    and for good reason. Too many ghosts. Spend enough time in there, and you\u2019ll
    start ta feel them\u2026 or so I\u2019ve observed. Listen, listen. You know,
    right? You shoulda figured it out sooner, you really shoulda. It\u2019s too late.
    None of us are makin\u2019 it out now. Sorry to Stella. Goodbye, Op.\""
  - ERROR
